# The old-channel thread and the injury rescue. Arc, owners and plants:
# content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.
# Thread owners (`who ow_*`) are cast once per voyage and never overlap.

card m_carrier
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 15 19
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when !is A ow_dose
text {A}'s ship-to-ship receiver, which still scans every channel any Mars craft ever used, logs a carrier too faint to see in any one sweep. Folded over a night at 10.96 seconds, 2.4 percent duty, it stands up out of the noise like a fence post. {A} files it under "retired hardware, probably".
do who ow_hail A
do mark t_carrier
do open dec_signal

card dec_signal
type decision
cat mystery
days 15 19
weight 5
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious open log
text The old-channel carrier is still there, patient as a dripping tap. {A} wants to answer it, if only to be polite: a plain hail on every pass. {B} points out that every hail turns the big dish off Earth for a few minutes, and the letters from home wait behind a conversation with a machine.
option open | Hail it every pass | {A} adds one line to the comms schedule: a plain hail on the old channel, every pass, until someone says stop. The first goes out at 14:02. Then static. The carrier comes and goes as before, and {A} logs the hail times to the second, out of habit.
  set signal_answered
  mark t_signal
  morale B -3
  trait A curious 5
option log | Log it, keep going | The carrier goes into the anomaly log under "later". {A} pins a printout of the folded trace above the bunk, just in case, and lets the dish stay on Earth.
  set signal_ignored
  mark t_signal
  morale A -5

card signal_reply
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 28 31
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when is A ow_hail
text At 03:12 the receiver catches something new on the old channel: half a frame of housekeeping in a format nobody has flown in years, cut off a byte before the field that says who sent it. The carrier's beat runs a fraction longer than it did. Mission Control answers eight minutes later: "say again."
do set signal_contact
do trait A curious 4

card signal_echo
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 28 31
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
text {A} pulls the old-channel carrier out of the receiver logs again, unasked. It's stronger now, the way anything gets louder as you close on it, and its period hasn't moved by a millisecond. The anomaly report uses the word "persistent", and leaves it there. {A} keeps the printout up.
do set echo_heard
do morale A -3

# Injury and rescue: needs supplies from another ship.
card crisis_eva
type event
cat grim
once
days 10 34
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
when kit_elsewhere A
text A micrometeoroid hits the hull during {A}'s EVA, a solo one with the ground watching on a delay, close enough to feel through the boots. {A} secures every tool, works back along the tether hand over hand, and comes inside with a wrist that won't bend.
do cond A injured
do who eva_who A
do morale A -10
do open rescue_kit

card rescue_kit
type rescue
cat grim
duration 1
roles A B
default volunteer
when cond A injured
when bestbond B A
text {A} needs the ultrasound and splint set from another ship's medical kit, and the next scheduled transfer window is days away.
option send | Send the kit | The fleet holds formation tight for an unscheduled transfer, and the kit rides the line across alone. {A}'s wrist is scanned and splinted by lunch, and the anomaly report runs to four pages.
  kit A
  res fuel -1
  morale A 6
option volunteer | {B} brings it over | {B} rides the line across with the kit in an unscheduled window and splints the wrist personally. The mission log calls it "nominal". Six ships read the log, and every one of them knows better.
  kitfrom B A
  move B A
  res fuel -1
  bond A B 12
  morale B 4
